---
description: Require actionable checklists in project Markdown plans
alwaysApply: true
---

# Planning documents

- When creating or substantially updating an implementation plan or project
  Markdown document, include actionable Markdown checkboxes (`- [ ]`).
- Use unchecked boxes for work that is not verified and checked boxes only for
  work completed with evidence.
- For verification checkboxes, record or link the command and result when the
  evidence is not obvious from the changed files.
- Do not mark full-suite, integration, or lint checks complete when they were
  not run successfully; distinguish unavailable tooling from a clean result.
- Recheck broad verification claims after later milestones change the codebase,
  and uncheck or annotate them when newer evidence invalidates the claim.
- Keep the checklist close to the relevant steps so it can be updated as work
  progresses.
- Do not commit or push planning-document changes without explicit user
  approval.
